course: dictionary
lesson: 10165
title: Names, borrowed words and short forms
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. A capital letter at the start of a word often means a name. «Your birthday is the date you were born, coming round again each year: Tia, born on 12 September 2016, turned 10 on 12 September 2026.» Tia is a girl's name here, because the sentence is about a person's birthday.
explain: Words from other languages can look like English words but mean something else. Tía in Spanish and tia in Portuguese both mean aunt, and they sound like TEE-uh. Tia is not an English word, so you will not find it in an ordinary English sentence with that meaning. Ask yourself: is this about a family member, a person's name, or something else?
explain: Some capital-letter words are short forms, called abbreviations. TIA stands for transient ischaemic attack, which is a mini-stroke. You will mostly see it in health writing, near words like doctor or hospital. It is not a name and it does not mean aunt. The context tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Tia is a girl's name.
fact: Tía (Spanish) and tia (Portuguese) mean aunt. Families with Spanish or Portuguese roots often call their aunt Tía, and their uncle Tío.
fact: TIA is an abbreviation for transient ischaemic attack, a mini-stroke.
fact: A TIA is a short warning stroke, and a person needs a doctor at once.
fact: A capital letter at the start of a word often means a name, but check the sentence to be sure.
exercise: «Tia, born on 12 September 2016, turned 10 on 12 September 2026.» In this sentence, what is Tia? | A date in September | An aunt in Spain | *A girl's name | A short warning stroke
exercise: In Spanish, what does tía mean? | A cake | Birthday | Mini-stroke | *Aunt
exercise: In a health text, what does TIA stand for? | A birthday card | Tía, the Spanish word for aunt | A girl's name | *Transient ischaemic attack, a mini-stroke
test: In a family with Spanish roots, what might a child call their aunt? | Tia's birthday | *Tía | Tío | TIA
test: A doctor reads «TIA» in a patient's notes. What does it probably mean? | *A mini-stroke, a short warning stroke | A girl called Tia | A birthday party | A Spanish dinner
exam: Which word means aunt in both Spanish and Portuguese? | Titan | Tiger | Tio | *Tia
